  "body": "Discover 16 Knights Road, Rothesay Bay - a solid mid-century home anchored on a spacious 1,012 sqm north-facing freehold site. \r\n\r\nOffering sea glimpses and excellent redevelopment potential under Mixed Housing Suburban zoning, this property blends immediate liveability with long-term upside. Whether you're dreaming of a refined renovation, multi-unit vision, or simply a coastal retreat with room to grow, this is a rare piece of Rothesay Bay real estate.\r\n\r\n\r\nProperty Highlights:\r\n\r\n* 1,012 sqm (more or less) north-facing land in coveted Mixed Housing Suburban Zone - ripe for development (subject to council approval)\r\n\r\n* Solid classic home built  - 1950's with three bedrooms, one bathroom, and a generous living area\r\n\r\n* Sea views & sunlight - elevated position captures coastal views and northern light\r\n\r\n* Walking distance to Rothesay Bay beach, local shops, and close to Murrays Bay amenities\r\n\r\n* Convenient access to motorway, Park & Ride, public transport, and just minutes to Albany and Massey University\r\n\r\n* Strong school zones including Murrays Bay Primary, Browns Bay Primary and Intermediate, Northcross, Rangitoto College\r\n\r\n* Solid title & freehold tenure, giving you certainty and flexibility\r\n\r\n* Land value uplift potential \r\n\r\n\r\nThis is not just a home -  it's a rare canvas in the heart of Rothesay Bay. You can move in and enjoy the coastal lifestyle as-is, breathe new life into the home, or explore its redevelopment possibilities permitted under current zoning. With sea views, broad sun exposure, excellent schools, and a neighbourhood that balances calm with connection, 16 Knights Road is an opportunity you won't see again soon.\r\n\r\nLet's talk about your options - from family haven to visionary investment.",
